<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RUT_Miasma_GradientAxisGenStep.xml   UtinniPatches - MIASMA_MECHANICS_1 M1 build pass

  Declares the GenStepDef for RM_GenStep_GradientAxis (already-spiked
  RM_MapComponent_GradientAxis's map-gen driver, this pass's own new class —
  src/RimMandrake/EnvironmentalHazards/Source/RM_GenStep_GradientAxis.cs).
  A GenStepDef on its own runs on no map (same pattern/comment as
  Defs/MapGeneration/JawaScrapfields.xml in this folder); registration is the
  separate Patches/RUT_Miasma_GradientAxis_Register.xml.

  order 225: after vanilla Terrain (210) and MutatorPostTerrain (220, both
  read from the live 1.6 Defs via RimSage this pass) — miasma_kit_spec.md
  M1's own text: "ordered after GenStep_Terrain".

  The class always records a salinity value for every cell on every map it
  runs on (harmless elsewhere), but only ever repaints terrain when the
  map's biome carries an RM_GradientAxisExtension — so registering it
  globally (see the Patches file) is safe for every OTHER biome too, not
  just the Miasma.

  MayRequire is load-bearing: genStep Class lives in
  mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards.
-->
<Defs>

  <GenStepDef MayRequire="mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards">
    <defName>RUT_GenStep_GradientAxis</defName>
    <order>225</order>
    <genStep Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.RM_GenStep_GradientAxis" />
  </GenStepDef>

</Defs>
